       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's a dangerous dose.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and a single 2,550 mg dose already equals the usual maximum for a whole day. At that dose the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis is serious, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day total, the usual maximum.\n- **Another dose or frequency**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg BID, or a lower titration dose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2550 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
